  "scope": "Fourteen drawn-layer scribe.5 records use a global sufficient size bound. After flattening reachable hierarchy and merging all touching/overlapping fragments, every connected feature must have at least one bounding-box side strictly below 10000 nm. Such a feature cannot contain a 10-by-10 um region at any location or orientation, so none can occur within 150 um of any scribe junction. A feature at exactly 10000 nm on both sides is a candidate. Large boxes, including thin L shapes and rings, stay unreviewed: bounding-box size does not prove a wide region or a nearby junction. No junction, frame, die or chip boundary is inferred. Empty drawing geometry is recorded separately. Generated-mask companion records and complete scribe context remain unreviewed; this report does not establish full physical coverage or process qualification.",
